ITEM GC  THE GREAT-CIRCLE LEAK: fix, and what it adds
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE FIX (in a private copy, gc/develop_spherical.py -- NOTHING in the repo was edited):
    cap = min(2*pi*d/n for (n,d) in nds)          # was inlined into hi0
    lo0, hi0 = 1e-7, cap - 1e-7
    prograde branch:  return [cap] if |f(cap)| <= 1e-9 else []      (was: [])
    retrograde branch: append cap to out when |f(cap)| <= 1e-9 and no root is already there
f's slope -> -infinity at the cap (alpha = pi - C*sqrt(cap-rho)), so a 1e-9 tolerance on f is
~1e-18 in rho: it cannot admit a non-root, and a genuine interior root can never be within 1e-7
of the cap without the bisection having found it. VERIFIED bit-exact: sin(cap/2) and
sin(pi*d/n) are the same double (scaling by 2 is exact), so ss == 1.0 exactly, asin gives pi/2,
